+# Privacy Audit — The Daily Grind website
+
+Last reviewed: 2026-11-09. Re-run this audit whenever a script, embed, font,
+image host, or form is added (check the DevTools Network panel / a HAR file
+for every request leaving our origin).
+
+## Third-party inventory
+
+| Origin | What | Data sent | Mitigation |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` | Homepage hero photo | Visitor IP + User-Agent (unavoidable for any fetch) | Loaded with `cross-origin(anonymous)` (no cookies) and `referrer-policy(no-referrer)`; document-level `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` as fallback; only third-party origin allowed by CSP `img-src` and `Connection-Allowlist`. **Follow-up:** self-host the image under `/assets/` and drop the origin from both policies. |
+
+No analytics, tag managers, advertising pixels, social SDKs, web fonts, or
+embeds are loaded. Any addition must be justified, listed here, and added
+explicitly to `_headers` — the CSP and `Connection-Allowlist` will block it
+otherwise.
+
+## Data minimization
+
+- The homepage collects no personal data and sets no cookies or storage.
+- `privacy.js` removes campaign/click identifiers (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`,
+  …) from the URL so they don't persist in history, bookmarks, or shared links.
+- No consent banner is shown because nothing non-essential is collected.
+  Privacy is the default, not an opt-in.
+
+## Headers (`_headers`, with `<meta>` fallbacks in `index.html`)
+
+- **Content-Security-Policy**: `default-src 'none'`, same-origin scripts and
+  styles only (inline CSS moved to `styles.css`), `form-action 'self'`,
+  `frame-ancestors 'none'`.
+- **Connection-Allowlist**: network-layer allowlist that also covers channels
+  CSP doesn't (preconnect, WebRTC, redirects). Chromium-only for now; CSP is the
+  cross-browser baseline.
+- **Referrer-Policy**: `strict-origin-when-cross-origin`.
+- **Permissions-Policy**: turns off camera, mic, geolocation, sensors, payment,
+  Topics, and similar powerful features.
+- **Clear-Site-Data** on `/logout` (`"cookies", "storage"`), and logout is now a
+  `POST` form, so a cross-site link or image can't sign users out.
+- `Cache-Control: private` on the personalized homepage.
+
+## Server-side requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- Session cookies: `Set-Cookie: session=…; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+  Never put tokens or PII in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`.
+- `/logout` must accept `POST` only and check `Origin` / a CSRF token.
+- Scrub emails, tokens, and IDs from logs; rate-limit account endpoints.
+- `/account/privacy` must offer self-service data export, correction, and
+  account deletion, and opting out must be as easy as signing up.
+- `/api/security-reports` receives CSP and Connection-Allowlist violation
+  reports. Store only the blocked URL and directive, not the full request.
